							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "-> humne useState hook ka use kiya hai to create a state variable called 'title' and a function called 'setTitle' to update the value of 'title'. The initial value of 'title' is set to an empty string. We have also defined a function called 'submitHandler' that will be called when the form is submitted. Inside this function, we log a message to the console and prevent the default form submission behavior using e.preventDefault()."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							}
						},
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "-> this is called two way binding because we are binding the value of the input field to the state variable 'title' and also updating the state variable 'title' when the input field value changes. This allows us to have a single source of truth for the input field value, which is the state variable 'title'. Whenever the user types something in the input field, it updates the state variable 'title', and whenever we update the state variable 'title', it updates the value of the input field. This is a common pattern in React for handling form inputs and keeping the UI in sync with the state."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
